      "settings": {
        "heading": "Already own one? Four checks, one minute.",
        "card_title": "Test yours in 60 seconds.",
        "copy": "<p><strong>1. The magnet.</strong> Hold a fridge magnet to the body, then to the cap separately. Copper is not magnetic. Any grip means steel under the finish — and the cap is usually where it shows up first.</p><p><strong>2. The interior.</strong> Torch, phone camera, look down the neck. Bare copper is the same reddish-brown inside as out. Silver, grey or glossy means lined or plated.</p><p><strong>3. The patina.</strong> If it has been in daily use for a month and the inside is still bright, it is not bare copper.</p><p><strong>4. The certificate.</strong> Ask your seller for a composition report for your batch. The answer you get — or don’t get — is the test.</p>",
        "closing": "Run all four on a Neera the day it arrives. We would rather invite the test than hope you skip it."
